# Playtest is the browser build

Friends and Nathan play https://nathan-elequin.itch.io/spinheritance-playtest

F5 in Godot on this repo **is** that same playtest game (`PlaytestFlag.on()` is true in the editor and in the Web Playtest export). Roster stays F6 in the editor.

## Ship (default, every fix)

Locked **2026-10-19**. Nathan does not quality-test before the playtest page updates. Keep doing this until he changes this rule.

After any change that friends would play (bug, overlay, card behavior, hub, Feedback, copy wiring, this checkout's game):

1. Export **Web Playtest** only (`build/web-playtest/index.html`).
2. `butler push` only to `nathan-elequin/spinheritance-playtest` (channel `html5`). The old `swipe-playtest` butler project is gone (itch page rename 2026-10-29).
3. Do it **in the same turn as the fix**. Do not wait for him to say ship, verify, F5, or “update itch.”

Worked examples of “ship immediately”: unplayable hotbar overlay, Bodyguard dying at 0 HP, Bushido dummy only on the second item.

## Do not

- Do not wait for a second message before exporting.
- Do not export the **Web** preset for friends.
- Do not `butler push` to `nathan-elequin/swipe` (the public page). That page is frozen unless Nathan says **promote** in that chat.
- Do not add `playtest` to `project.godot` features (that would bake into every export).

## Local Play (Cherry PC)

No extra Godot setting. Stop Play if it is already running, then F5. You should get the playtest hub (Brand New / Middle Progress / Continue / Feedback). F2 is Feedback. F6 is still Roster.
